title: Denial Intelligence › Deadlines › Overdue denials
route: /denials/D-3318
intro: What changes, and what still works, once a window has run out. Example: D-3318's peer-to-peer window after fast-forwarding 2 days, then a written-appeal deadline that has passed.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: nothing blocks filing after a deadline. Call times are offered only after the demo clock, so once the window has run out there is none to book.
---
start s1 "Peer-to-peer window of D-3318 has run out (Demo menu: fast-forward 2 days)"
screen sc1 "List row moves to the top with the pill 'Window closed' (red)\nHeader pill 'Peer-to-peer window closed' (red)"
process p1 "'Written appeal' becomes 'Recommended'\nThe peer-to-peer card is no longer chosen first"

click c1 "Click the 'Peer-to-peer call' card"
toast t1 "'The peer-to-peer window has closed'\n'A written appeal is still open.'"
process p2 "The card is not selected"

click c2 "Click 'Change the time' (the peer-to-peer choice)"
overlay o1 "Modal 'Confirm the next step: peer-to-peer call'"
decision d1 "Is any call time left? (starts after the demo clock, before the window closes)"
toast t2 "'No call time is left inside the payer's window. Choose a written appeal instead.'\nConfirm is greyed out"
process p3 "Only while the window is still open: the times offered are ahead of the clock\nThe call can be booked"
click c3 "Click 'Cancel', the X, press Esc, or click the dimmed area"
endx e1 "Nothing changes"

click c4 "Click 'Open the brief'"
screen b1 "Brief page: 'Closes in' reads 'Closed' in red\n'Key dates' still lists 'Peer-to-peer window closes'"
click c5 "Click 'Record the call outcome'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Peer-to-peer › Record the call outcome"

start s2 "A written-appeal or resubmission deadline has run out (example D-3301 after 42 days, D-3290 after 6 days)"
screen sc2 "List pill 'Window closed' (red)\nHeader pill 'Appeal deadline passed' or 'Resubmission window closed' (red)"
screen o2 "'Written appeal' card reads 'Deadline passed' in place of the time to file or resubmit\nStill 'Recommended'"
click c6 "Click 'Draft the appeal', or 'Open the draft'"
process p4 "Drafting, signing and filing work as usual\nDrawer sub line still says 'Due 11/30.'\nNo late warning (demo)"
goto g2 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Written appeal › Confirm and draft"
process p5 "Filed appeals have no deadline of ours, so they never turn overdue"

s1 --> sc1 --> p1
sc1 --> c1 --> t1 --> p2
sc1 --> c2 --> o1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| t2 --> c3
d1 -->|Yes| p3 --> c3
c3 --> e1
sc1 --> c4 --> b1 --> c5 --> g1
s2 --> sc2 --> o2 --> c6 --> p4 --> g2
sc2 -.-> p5
